        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_error": null,
        "superseded_justification": "MIMIC-on-FHIR does not populate MedicationAdministration.identifier.value with inputevents.linkorderid; the ICU ETL neither selects nor writes that field (mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_medication_administration_icu.sql:7-23,42-100), so the declared typed NULL explains the linkorderid gap. The remaining key substitution and endtime conflict are intrinsic: lines 8-9 cast source start/end through TIMESTAMPTZ, lines 61-65 write only those transformed values to MedicationAdministration.effectivePeriod, and line 20 creates an opaque timestamp-free UUID. Source 2165-03-10 02:28 is irreversibly normalized to 03:28 in the America/New_York spring-forward gap and cannot be distinguished from a genuine 03:28 by any FHIR query. The attributed conflict is 1/8513 (0.0117%), consistent with DST-gap rarity. Representable fidelity is 8511/8513 (99.9765%), excluding linkorderid.",
